      "projects": [
        {
          "title": "VEHICLE THEFT DETECTION AND CONTROL",
          "subtitle": "Apr 2017 - Apr 2017",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "1. The project consists of two modes a)Drive Mode b)Theft Mode\n2. When the Drive Mode is switched ON, the automobile is in its regular operation and is switched OFF \n     when the ignition is turned OFF\n3. The Automobile is switched to Theft Mode when the automobile is parked.\n4. If the Drive Mode is turned ON in this mode then a message is sent to the owner of the automobile \n    indicating that the vehicle is accessed by someone else.\n5. If the owner resends a message with 'STOP' then the vehicle stops and a message to the owner is \n    again sent back with the GPS co-ordinates.\n"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "ONE-BIT DAC",
          "subtitle": "Feb 2017 - Feb 2017",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "1. The MP3 is decoded in the first step.\n2. The decoded MP3 i.e PCM data is transmitted to FPGA using serial port.\n3. PWM siganl is smoothened out to create an analog input through sigma-delta modulator.\n4. DAC is required to connect FPGA to a speaker.\n5. VHDL is used to program the FPGA.\n6. CYCLONE FPGA DEO-NANO dev kit is used."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "OBSTACLE AVOIDING AUTONOMOUS ROBOT",
          "subtitle": "Jan 2017 - Jan 2017",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "1. Objective of the Robot is to detect the obstacle, measure the distance towards its left and right \n     direction     and move to the direction where the next obstacle is at larger distance.\n2. Ultrasonic sensor is mounted on a servo motor to measure the distance.\n3. Motor driver L298 is used to drive 2 DC motors.\n4. Platform used is Raspberry Pi and Python is used to code the whole process\n5. VPython is used for simulation process."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Modelling of Parking Gate Controller using Atmega328 micro-controller and simulation in VPython",
          "subtitle": "Dec 2016 - Dec 2016",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "This project emphasizes about a new approach in the field of parking gate system. Atmel based microcontroller is used to control the whole operation. The new design eliminates the use of any physical devices, buttons and knobs to open the parking gate. The objective is to detect only the automobile and open the gate.\nThe system is designed using Arduino microcontroller embedded system and the design is done using its Integrated Development Environment and embedded C. \n1. Distance sensors are used to detect the vehicle if it is moving from the parking lot to outside.\n2. This narrows the detection of any other obstacles since more than one ultrasonic distance senor is \n     used.\n3. RF Transmitter and Receiver is also interfaced to this system for the convenience.\n4. VPython is used to virtually create the whole scenario and synchronized with the controller to show \n    the operation.\n5. The system is implemented in real time. "
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "DESIGN AND IMPLEMENTAION OF 32-BIT SDRAM CONTROLLER USING VERILOG",
          "subtitle": "Nov 2016 - Nov 2016",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
